      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is completely understandable that suggesting small hobbies feels dismissive when you are experiencing such a profound sense of loss. When the core feels gone, that feeling of futility is a very real and valid response to grief. Rather than looking for a grand new story, perhaps exploring narratives about survival and reinvention—even those written by others—could offer a gentler perspective on moving through the aftermath. Please remember that even when things feel burned down, there is always the possibility of rebuilding, much like soil after a fire.",
